# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Grant group "rapl" read access to the RAPL energy counters.
#
# Since Linux 5.10 (CVE-2020-8694, "PLATYPUS") every powercap zone's
# energy_uj attribute is mode 0400 root, because reading it at a high rate
# is a power side channel. The other files node_exporter's rapl collector
# reads per zone (name, max_energy_range_uj) are 0444 already.
#
# Every zone and sub-zone (intel-rapl:0, intel-rapl:0:0, intel-rapl:1, ...,
# and intel-rapl-mmio:* where present) is its own powercap device, so one
# rule covers all of them; the parent control-type device (intel-rapl) has
# no energy_uj and is skipped by the ATTR match. AMD Zen exposes the same
# intel-rapl:* names through intel_rapl_common.
#
# sysfs attributes are not device nodes, so udev's GROUP= and MODE= keys do
# not apply to them, and a RUN+= chgrp/chmod would execute in the udev_t
# SELinux domain, which under the stock targeted policy may read and write
# sysfs files but not change their attributes. Instead each matching zone
# is handed to systemd: the template name in SYSTEMD_WANTS is instantiated
# with the zone's escaped sysfs path, and that instance applies the group
# and mode as root. systemd re-runs an inactive wanted unit on every add
# event, so a reload of the intel_rapl_* modules and the udevadm trigger in
# the package scriptlet re-apply the permissions as well.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="powercap", ATTR{energy_uj}=="?*", \
  TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="prometheus-node-exporter-rapl@.service"
